7. Important sandbox diagnosis and fix
Initially:

4KHDHub worked alone.

Combined requests returned CNO and PressPlay but omitted 4KHDHub.

User supplied actual Render logs.

Observed:

Isolated 4KHDHub extraction completed in about 10.30 seconds with three links.

Combined 4KHDHub extractions hit provider_timeout at approximately 20.34 and 20.82 seconds.

PressPlay launched Chromium and took roughly 33–42 seconds overall.

Castle also timed out.

CNO was substantially slower under combined load.

The batch itself completed normally; completed:4 meant four tasks settled, not four successful sources.

Conclusion:

Immediate cause of missing 4KHDHub results: worker timeout before extraction completed.

Resource contention was the likely explanation for the combined-request slowdown, not proven down to a specific CPU/memory/network resource.

Do not misstate the cause as Nuvio hiding results or resolution filtering.

Implemented sandbox scheduling fix:

At most two non-browser extractions simultaneously.

PressPlay runs after queued non-browser work.

PressPlay is exclusive within the service process, including across requests.

No browser extraction overlaps other provider extraction tasks.

Existing playback logic/timeouts retained.

Commit:
5150bd769068130f300f5c6478153d63c0262c83

User then confirmed CNO, 4KHDHub, and PressPlay all appeared in Nuvio.

